 {:db/id "q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236" :answer-field/id #uuid "39de4ad4-8ca2-5e4e-a502-b05807674875" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" "q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236/dd44173d16ac132df1a97f9fe2611d3e6d5e55380c00e64a71bded7896fbc16d" "q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236/0b305abae202a2af6d703a8ffcc92c0a2279d01fc874b7aff5d842eca112db9a" "q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236/861981e024e897416682817ca9e79c6d1e8ed9b541c7efe134d14879c4bffd37" "q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf"] :answer-field/correct "q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236/0b305abae202a2af6d703a8ffcc92c0a2279d01fc874b7aff5d842eca112db9a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-111789" :question/id #uuid "96dc0ffa-c035-5c4a-b42f-7a4928dfb8df" :question/math-academy-id "q-111789" :question/problem "Let\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nbe the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ Then $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $T$ has proportional rows, and yet $T$ is not the zero matrix. \n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=1$ and $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line that passes through the origin.\n\nMoreover, the line must pass through the origin $(0,0)$ and the point $(2,-1),$ which is defined by the (repeated) columns of the matrix $T.$ \n\nComputing the slope $m$ of this line, we get\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-1-0}{2-0}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111789/ma-source-field/ad8f9a9800940419e4e81b51e05e28c1dc9ba3bfda62382aa3c9a633520ab236"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
