 {:db/id "q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d582062-813e-5b4d-b116-6b4cb9d5d390" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa/0782ac8d667d956fe0ee1d6f323d66fcdaa32119b1cf285f31f497d2b2f57132" "q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa/ddc30c9cd25aa4c83dd80fbffa268bafec24e6eac8403d004741b24a5813fe37" "q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa/0a193d250e974687a3d07c190e91ec5e709e0b3361e7f508e79d731cb4fd27b5" "q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa/862a60fa21b17f3de998a3ab1413d0bbb8b7f8af32d4495ac7c7a59c39236638" "q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa/5d7255b1e6d0ed12751dd0eb1f28e93112ef78b006a3e44c8c5c4d27e8897f24"] :answer-field/correct "q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa/0a193d250e974687a3d07c190e91ec5e709e0b3361e7f508e79d731cb4fd27b5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-113502" :question/id #uuid "201b1303-edfe-5a94-b70a-3687fd03d284" :question/math-academy-id "q-113502" :question/problem "$\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =18(2-5x)^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113502/ma-source-field/9ecd37f5b7334b05c2ca95cc64f63754426e4cc7d8c79d7f0f72b6ce560ca8fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
