 {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbaa4a7f-8da9-5213-ac9e-71081f8e7d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/565166cf63c6bd9dbac0d04ca61a0c6f981978aa7e6bc0ef8c867c62d6a1bb9b" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/61f3f3c6f85611206c2aff87c729df9061c4ff37512598c40317327f624da63a" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/24cc054f51407bd5127f81290b93dc0d4174045b75296455bc29b916953efe66" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/06b1934ddad28062c907dac0d6301b6d874acae263494e4e79b10349b52af175" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/4ff5c6a42cb789a6a2e859ea420445b0ed532439c8a9bb0fd4d1ca25e6c99279"] :answer-field/correct "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/24cc054f51407bd5127f81290b93dc0d4174045b75296455bc29b916953efe66" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-116755" :question/id #uuid "9352ab9c-fd90-5378-93d7-0236e8a891cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-116755" :question/problem "![](images/ac/acef9493a9569c023c00e67323f1ffbe8d2f424796205deafb69214838b2c4e2.png)\n\nWater is being poured into a rectangular prism shaped tank. The length and width of this tank are $8\\text{ m}$ and $4\\text{ m},$ respectively. If the height of the water increases at a rate of $0.25\\text{ m/hour}$, determine the rate at which the volume of stored water increases." :question/worked-solution "We define the following variables:\n\n- let $L$ and $W$ be the length and width of the tank, respectively, and\n\n- let $h$ and $V$ be the height and volume of the water in the tank, respectively.\n\nNote that $h$ and $V$ change with time, while $L$ and $W$ are constants. \n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nL=8\\,\\text{m},\\,W=4\\,\\text{m},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{hour}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the two time-dependent variables, $V$ and $h,$ is given by the formula for the volume of the water in the tank:\n\n$$\nV=LWh\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides with respect to $t,$ treating both $L$ and $W$ as constants, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWh) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =LW\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(8)(4)\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =32\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water level is rising at a rate of $8\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
