 {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "0aeaedd6-8135-5962-8437-2a69c460095e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/bb15a40c16849e14349d04337998509e2e5dd918546f76a1e7ff128017e5344d" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/02b21ed2f804e40681c56d757dc3f9c750b444c33d6d36e41df2ee528dd431a1" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/ae53b6f2c3582ddd63640d3f6763e2017e3abb6e1a778011c7960c79751074ce" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/7caaf868888dca20a3cc9e96f97a6bb9a68503c0024c12e93ca091ec0363e142" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/2f21e4ef22a71dee952e750116fe1cd7727568cfcc4456ac810b94fe1d8b222f"] :answer-field/correct "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/bb15a40c16849e14349d04337998509e2e5dd918546f76a1e7ff128017e5344d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-118442" :question/id #uuid "e694bf71-afc9-51ff-82ce-ddde47237115" :question/math-academy-id "q-118442" :question/problem "![](images/99/997eb5cc08dcff78cb32f5b47b5d066546854b05f3b066953772e456e713d773.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could be used to describe the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/1e/1e532c806d81c3c4015d78f814dc4ea3fc3483f22d34ade385894df2e8e7e3c5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=5sin⁡(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n5sin⁡(-x)=-5sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-5sin⁡x.$ However, $y=-5sin⁡x$ is not among the given options." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
