 {:db/id "q-118443" :question/id #uuid "ef71e5dd-2133-5139-bcc4-313a9e867ac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-118443" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f012ee5880b4ec6c4c2cad4aa44da672b789f21c7f9969dcec50a25596e47c4b.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could be used to describe the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/bc/bc61bf27fb210e0dc849829d5c287936fcb3f73bc279e98af8a64ba4085b8309.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $6.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=6sin⁡(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n6sin⁡(-x)=-6sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-6sin⁡x.$ However, $y=-6sin⁡x$ is not among the given options." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
