 {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685" :answer-field/id #uuid "34d0bc62-23d7-51e0-a40e-82b353c65411" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/25d79eef8a16f080073a8e877263e916b245aa7f9e3282b422f7b7d7005baf31" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e"] :answer-field/correct "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/25d79eef8a16f080073a8e877263e916b245aa7f9e3282b422f7b7d7005baf31" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-120911" :question/id #uuid "13b68e5e-22d6-5fa0-a4a4-6c5d1f4c0a70" :question/math-academy-id "q-120911" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x\\sqrt{y},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with three steps of equal size to approximate $y(3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(3).$ The distance from $x=0$ and $x=3$ is $3,$ and since we are asked to use three steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(0)=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=1\\cdot \\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot 1=1 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+1=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ |\n| $3$ | $2+2\\sqrt{2}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(3)≈2+2\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
