 {:db/id "q-125561" :question/id #uuid "8904abf3-dbf2-549a-8f8b-9fbdb7308ad3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125561" :question/problem "Find the entry ${e}_{31}$ of the matrix $E$, where \n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry ${e}_{31}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $1$st column. Therefore, ${e}_{31}=-3.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125561/ma-source-field/1a9a5f0e5ee7e9df5b1d2659d1158abf2767686e7cef2b8ab811bc27b2557a20"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
