 {:db/id "q-125593" :question/id #uuid "5aee8772-02f1-5e96-b1e0-f67b0c259d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-125593" :question/problem "Find the entry ${r}_{43}$ of the matrix $R$, where \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry ${r}_{43}$ lies at the intersection of the $4$th row and $3$rd column. Therefore, ${r}_{43}=1.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125593/ma-source-field/6831f863eb5f497c8eb9a540ce30078c6d68ed9ca6550a16bd37a3ddead4ddc6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
