 {:db/id "q-127003" :question/id #uuid "4fcf1fe7-fb4f-5cde-8368-06562ddf512e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127003" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4t \\\\ y=-7+3t \\\\ z=9-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-4t \\\\ -7+3t \\\\ 9-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4t \\\\ 3t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,-7,9)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127003/ma-source-field/e1ce45116c2f64902a2dd0e180450afeba3efbf3588d38ebcae4a4796213ad1f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
