 {:db/id "q-127033" :question/id #uuid "82e0d9c4-429c-5e53-bd8d-068f50a3ec35" :question/math-academy-id "q-127033" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3+7t \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=1-5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+7t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1-5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(-3,0,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127033/ma-source-field/bfcc0e096b781e2436a7e4b575c2ad5d7c02cb07f5bb4b0daa853d70ff6277cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
